<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="no"?>
<!-- =====================================================================
     PRJEDU_hardening - AyMON example: harden a plant that was delivered
     with a weak configuration, for a security course.

     PLT/S00 is a small plant - a tank, a pump, a high-level trip, a
     recipe - with a page and live values on 127.0.0.1:8101. It works.
     It was also set up in a hurry: its access configuration has seven
     weaknesses. The task is to find them and fix them in db_PLT.xml.

     Two tools help, both on the page:
       SELF-CHECK   the plant reads its own configuration and names what
                    it can see there (main.self_check, every 5 s)
       ACCESS TEST  the page logs in as four identities - no user name,
                    a monitor, an operator, an engineer - and tries what
                    each may and may not do
     A weakness is fixed when both say so.

     db_PLT_solution.xml is one way to fix all seven; AyXDB_solution.xml
     runs it (run_solution.bat). Try it yourself first.

     Two connections, two documents: inside the FREE edition.

     Run:  run.bat,  then open  http://127.0.0.1:8101/
     ===================================================================== -->
<xdb id="XDB" xdb_lib="AyPRO" xdb_log="4" log_cfg="0x39C0" log_lnk="%PRJ%/log/XDB.log"
     sta="0x0300" tid="S01">
	<config>
		<doc id="PLT/S00" sta="0x0300" src="%DB%/db_PLT.xml" desc="the plant, as delivered" />
	</config>
	<data>
	</data>
</xdb>
